cases.finalMessage:
I've sent the def14a parser merge to a gemini farm-out running in the `sync-origin` worktree; it hasn't reported back yet. It will:
- keep local main's side of the scoring files (`score.py`, `thresholds.json`, `lock.sha256`, the regression-set builder, `run_baseline.sh`, `GRIND_PLAN.md`), since that is what the local gold data is hashed for;
- combine both grinds' fixes in the five Go parser files, 29 conflict blocks in all;
- rebuild the parser binary.

It has to show four things for the merge to count:
- no conflict markers left;
- `go vet` and `go test` pass, with every test from both sides present;
- the binary rebuilds;
- a local scoring round of the merged parser has no gated metric worse than a round of local main's parser.

Both rounds write to their own directories, so the live grind's output in `/data/def14a_own/work` is untouched.

The local grind is still running and keeps merging into local main. Once this merge lands, `sync-origin` will need local main merged into it once more to pick up whatever the grind has added since. A background wait will wake me when the report is written.

